# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, files committed from a Windows checkout land with CRLF, and Prettier — which
# defaults to `endOfLine: "lf"` — fails `format:check` on them in CI. That is what turned the `ci`
# workflow red on main: the content was fine, the bytes were not.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores every text file with LF and checks it out with LF on every platform, so
# the working tree and the committed blob agree no matter who wrote the file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Deployment manifests are rewritten by the publish workflow on every image build, so normalising
# them here would collide with that bot on every deploy — a rebase for line endings nobody reads.
# Left exactly as written; nothing lints them, and the workflow that owns them runs on Linux.
deploy/** -text

# Binary files must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.qcow2 binary
